<launch>
  <!-- vitulus_ui / Phase 1: Visual Odometry from the d435 (RGB-D).
       SHADOW SOURCE ONLY: this node ONLY publishes an odometry topic
       (/vo/odom) + quality info (/vo/odom_info). publish_tf is FALSE so it
       does NOT touch the live odom->base_link TF produced by navi_transform.
       It is meant to be consumed by navi_transform as a gated bridge source
       during GPS-denied stretches (daylight; it degrades at night - that is
       handled by the consumer's confidence gate, not here).

       Run standalone for validation:
         roslaunch vitulus_navi vo_rgbd_odometry.launch
       then inspect /vo/odom and /vo/odom_info (Vis/inliers, lost). -->

  <arg name="camera"        default="d435"/>
  <arg name="frame_id"      default="base_link"/>
  <arg name="approx_sync"   default="true"/>

  <node pkg="rtabmap_odom" type="rgbd_odometry" name="vo_rgbd_odometry" output="screen" respawn="true" respawn_delay="3">
    <remap from="rgb/image"        to="/$(arg camera)/color/image_raw"/>
    <remap from="depth/image"      to="/$(arg camera)/aligned_depth_to_color/image_raw"/>
    <remap from="rgb/camera_info"  to="/$(arg camera)/color/camera_info"/>
    <remap from="odom"             to="/vo/odom"/>
    <remap from="odom_info"        to="/vo/odom_info"/>

    <param name="frame_id"          type="string" value="$(arg frame_id)"/>
    <!-- isolated odom frame; never published as TF -->
    <param name="odom_frame_id"     type="string" value="vo_odom"/>
    <param name="publish_tf"        type="bool"   value="false"/>
    <param name="approx_sync"       type="bool"   value="$(arg approx_sync)"/>
    <!-- 2026-07-11: was 0.2. On the auto-reset path (OdometryROS.cpp:850,
         getTransform(odom_frame_id=vo_odom, base_link)), rtabmap blocks up to
         this duration. Because publish_tf=false, vo_odom is NEVER in TF, so that
         lookup can NEVER succeed and always burns the full wait before the reset
         fires. In daylight (pose not null) the reset path is not entered, so this
         costs nothing; at night pose goes null often (ResetCountdown=1, so one
         null frame = one reset) and every such frame paid +0.2s AND emitted the
         "Could not get transform from vo_odom to base_link ... does not exist"
         warning seen in night logs (814 warns == 814 resets, lost=0). Set to 0.0
         so the failing lookup returns immediately; RTAB-Map then resets to its
         own latest computed pose, which is exactly what we want. The static
         base_link to camera_link TF (real, published) is looked up on a separate
         path that already resolves instantly, so 0.0 does not starve it. -->
    <param name="wait_for_transform_duration" type="double" value="0.0"/>

    <!-- Auto-reset after losing tracking so the node ALWAYS recovers when good
         conditions return. With 0 (no reset) it stayed lost forever after a
         single bad patch (e.g. sun / open area), so it never came back in the
         shade. The consumer (navi_transform bridge) absorbs the reset jump: it
         only uses this source while gated (low covariance) and refreshes its
         reference every cycle. -->
    <param name="Odom/ResetCountdown" type="string" value="1"/>
    <param name="Odom/Holonomic"      type="string" value="false"/>
    <param name="Reg/Force3DoF"       type="string" value="true"/>
    <param name="Vis/EstimationType"  type="string" value="1"/>   <!-- PnP (3D->2D) -->
    <param name="Vis/MinInliers"      type="string" value="15"/>

    <!-- ===== 2026-07-11 THROUGHPUT TUNE (daylight compute-bound) =====
      BASELINE (measured daylight, robot parked/moving, 15 fps color+depth in):
        /vo/odom publishes only ~4.4 Hz  (interval 0.20-0.33 s)
        odom_info timeEstimation = 0.19-0.30 s  (this is the bottleneck, CPU 79%)
        localBundleTime ~0.09 s, localMapSize=2000, localKeyFrames~1787
        quality EXCELLENT: features ~866, matches ~483, inliers ~318,
        pose cov ~3.9e-5, lost=False.
      ROOT CAUSE of 4.4 Hz: NOT the TF wait (reset path not entered in daylight,
        0 resets this session). It is pure per-frame compute in feature
        detect+describe+PnP+local bundle adjustment over a 2000-word local map.
      LEVER (one, conservative): Vis/MaxFeatures 1000 to 600.
        Fewer keypoints to detect/describe (GFTT/ORB), match, RANSAC-PnP and
        bundle-adjust. With inliers currently ~318 (far above MinInliers=15)
        there is huge headroom; ~40% fewer features should still leave over 150
        inliers while cutting the dominant detect/match/BA cost. Expected:
        timeEstimation toward ~0.13-0.16 s giving ~6-8 Hz; combined with wait=0.0
        removing the night 0.2 s/frame reset stall, target 10 Hz or more is
        plausible.
      NOT CHANGED (documented follow-up levers if 600 is not enough, change ONE
        at a time and re-measure): OdomF2M/MaxSize 2000 to 1000 (smaller local
        map = less BA, mild drift risk), Odom/ImageDecimation 1 to 2 (halves
        detect cost, coarser depth), OdomF2M/BundleAdjustmentMaxFrames 10 to 5.
      KEEP (do not touch): publish_tf=false, Odom/ResetCountdown=1,
        Reg/Force3DoF=true, Odom/Holonomic=false, Vis/EstimationType=1.
      RE-MEASURE CHECKLIST after restart:
        1) rostopic echo -n5 /vo/odom_info | grep -E 'timeEstimation|inliers|features'
           expect timeEstimation below 0.16 s, inliers still above ~120.
        2) rostopic hz /vo/odom  target 10 Hz or more.
        3) grep current node log for 'Could not get transform from vo_odom'
           and 'automatically reset': expect none in daylight; at night the
           reset may still occur but must no longer add 0.2 s (wait=0.0).
        4) parked twist noise sanity: vyaw std ~0.0014 rad/s (see plan note).
    ===== -->
    <param name="Vis/MaxFeatures"     type="string" value="600"/>
    <!-- 2026-07-11 second lever: smaller F2M local map (bundle time ~0.09s over
         2000 words was the other half of the compute cost). -->
    <param name="OdomF2M/MaxSize"     type="string" value="1000"/>
  </node>
</launch>
